{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/493625-mass-combat","id":493625,"title":"mass combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-27T08:03:51-07:00","id":493625,"title":"mass combat","content":"So I have a player who wants to play more of a big general type, coming up with battle plans and raids, more the sitting back and barking orders then in the thick of it....any recommendations on how to go about rolling that out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:15:01-07:00","id":493685,"title":"","content":"Step 1: Become Athro.<br /> Step 2: Lead Battles.<br /> Step 3: Profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:26:26-07:00","id":493765,"title":"","content":"I meant crunch, what dice pools and system and what not....I don't want to just hand victory over to him or dash his hopes against the rocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T11:35:29-07:00","id":493768,"title":"","content":"I am unfortunately at work so I don't have my books handy but I believe Dark Ages: Vampire Storyteller Companion had rules for large scale combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T12:16:14-07:00","id":493844,"title":"","content":"Opposing Attribute + Leadership rolls, adjusted for factors like morale, fatigue, placement advantages, etc. Make it an extended roll, like with chasing down another character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T13:23:26-07:00","id":493907,"title":"","content":"I need to look at the rules in DA:V because that sounds interesting. If you're okay with wargames and you've played Warhammer you could probably lean in that direction...one pack = one unit, which loses members as it takes damage.<br /> <br /> I did this once before back in college and it was something like... Give each pack attack/hit/resist/rage based loosely on their average physical stats and abilities. Do something like &quot;roll hit + pack members still standing -&gt; successes is how many hits they get in for attack damage; roll resist to subtract damage, every full multiple of 5 damage left over, someone dies&quot; and scale the numbers until it's as lethal as you want it. No wounds. Spend a rage to double-move, or guarantee +1 attack lands, or to get a roll to rage-heal a pack member that was going to die. Leader rolls leadership every round and can hand out # of successes as rage points to different packs.<br /> <br /> Some powers (razor claws, spirit of the fray) you can just abstract by adding a point to the pack's stats. Big important one-shot ones, write up rules ahead of time and let the pack use it in addition to their normal action as many times as feels appropriate. If you want to add ranged weapons...well, we're already really stretching the limits of the system, and it's going to not be Werewolf very soon. I dunno, roll hit + figures, diff modified by range. Adjust the damage threshold for attacks based on the kind of damage involved (werewolves soaking lead bullets, need 8 damage in one attack to kill someone; squishy humans soaking claws, each 2 damage will kill someone). Stats in the 1-5 range are probably okay.<br /> <br /> ...I don't think most people are going to want to play Garouhammer, but if you want a one-shot vignette for a real meatgrinder scenario like a massive attack against a Sept, well, maybe. A system like this is just good for two things: &quot;I want to see large armies of Garou die horribly&quot;, and &quot;I'm committed to playing out this battle scene but it would take too long.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T13:25:21-07:00","id":493910,"title":"","content":"add tactical components like divide the battleground in section, each section has a battle plan and rolls differently, this way the &quot;allied forces&quot; can prevail in a section, lose in another and so on; and, by the way, account differently the different enemies the garou can face, for example:<br /> Sector A: Silver Pack VS BSD pack<br /> Sector B: 2 Mixed Garou Pack VS 4 First Team<br /> Sector C: Bone Gnawers pack and well armed Kins VS Fomori wardens<br /> Sector D: Nosferatu allies VS Pentex/Sabbat Vampires<br /> <br /> each section account for different problems, and should be dealt differently","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T21:00:08-07:00","id":593500,"title":"","content":"Mass Combat?<br /> <br /> Fighting in Church again....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:09:36-07:00","id":594013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf-Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/493625-mass-combat?p=593500#post593500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-r